## Tools from an API description

An integration can name an OpenAPI or GraphQL description instead of writing each tool out. Spotlight generates a tool for each operation `tools.include` and `tools.exclude` leave in. It reads the description when the integration is created, and again when its `url`, `document`, `baseUrl`, `revision`, `depth` or kind of `auth` (`oauth2` or `secrets`) changes, on any update after a failed read, and when the integration's host is connected over OAuth. Calling a tool never reads it. `tools.approval` asks a person before a tool runs, or with `false` lets it run without asking.

{{ tffile "examples/resources/spotlight_integration/petstore.tf" }}

The generated tools are known only after apply, so `tools` reads `(known after apply)` in the plan. A generated tool named through `tools["…"]` that the description does not offer fails the apply, not the plan. When a later read fails, the tools from the last good read stay offered: `described.hash` keeps that read, and `described.problem` says why the latest one failed.

